+### Optional checkpoint entry-button label (v54)
+
+A checkpoint may include `openLabel`, an authored plain-text label for its
+entry button, for example `"openLabel": "πήγαινε στο συνεργείο"`. It is trimmed
+and must contain 1–100 characters; invalid, blank or overlong values are omitted
+and use the normal localized entry label. The label is rendered with
+`textContent`, never HTML. Omit the field to retain the existing GR/EN default.
+Completed checkpoints retain the existing localized revisit label.
+The field lives inside the checkpoint specification, so normal validation,
+Update, duplicate, export and import preserve it without adding a default
+property to legacy checkpoints. It changes no question, answer or gate rule.
